From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: use extended CPU retention state

The SM8750 CPU idle states currently pass the legacy PSCI value 0x4.
Qualcomm's newer arm64 device trees describe the corresponding rail/CPU
retention state with the extended value 0x40000004. On the Odin 3, the
legacy state enters suspend but does not return from s2idle, while WFI
remains wakeable.

Use the extended state encoding for both SM8750 clusters. This keeps the
existing hierarchy and latency values intact while selecting the encoding
used by the other recent Qualcomm platforms.

This is a diagnostic and functional fix for firmware that distinguishes
the legacy and extended state encodings.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
index 735e7628df96..armada000000 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750.dtsi
@@ -180,15 +180,15 @@
 				compatible = "arm,idle-state";
 				idle-state-name = "ret";
-				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x00000004>;
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x40000004>;
 				entry-latency-us = <93>;
 				exit-latency-us = <129>;
 				min-residency-us = <560>;
 			};
 
 			cluster1_c4: cpu-sleep-1 {
 				compatible = "arm,idle-state";
 				idle-state-name = "ret";
-				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x00000004>;
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x40000004>;
 				entry-latency-us = <172>;
 				exit-latency-us = <130>;
 				min-residency-us = <686>;
